# ==============================================================================
# MyComputerAgent Environment Configuration Example
#
# NOTE: This file is a reference only — MCA does NOT load .env files itself.
# To use these variables, export them in the shell that launches `mca`
# (e.g. `set -a; source .env; set +a`). They take precedence over Settings keys
# and are never persisted.
#
# All API keys are completely optional!
# Recording, local search, and offline semantic UI grounding work without any keys.
#
# RECOMMENDATION: Instead of saving keys in this file, you can securely enter them
# inside the running app via Menu Bar (✨) ▸ Settings ▸ Models & Keys.
# Keys entered in Settings are encrypted using Apple's Secure Enclave (HPKE RFC 9180)
# and never stored on disk in plaintext.
# ==============================================================================

# Google Gemini API Key
# Used for: Gemini Flash batch audio transcription and Gemini reasoning/live chat.
# Get your key at: https://aistudio.google.com/
GEMINI_API_KEY=your_gemini_api_key_here
# GOOGLE_API_KEY=your_google_api_key_here

# Anthropic Claude API Key
# Used for: Claude multimodal reasoning and desktop computer use.
# Get your key at: https://console.anthropic.com/
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=your_anthropic_api_key_here

# OpenAI API Key (or OpenAI-compatible service)
# Used for: OpenAI-compatible chat and reasoning.
# Get your key at: https://platform.openai.com/
OPENAI_API_KEY=your_openai_api_key_here

# TypeSafe AI API Key
# Used for: Ultra-low latency (<200ms) System One Jev model for desktop GUI grounding.
# When omitted, MCA automatically falls back to deterministic local semantic grounding.
# Get your key at: https://typesafe.ai/
TYPESAFE_API_KEY=your_typesafe_api_key_here
